-- title:
--   Bounded pieces M_{n,m} are projective over W(k)/p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon W(\mathbb F_{p^2})\to W(k)$, and a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ (a two-dimensional formal group law with a $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$-action and an endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[a^{\mathrm{Fr}}]\circ\varpi$) over $W(k)/pW(k)$, assumed special for the structure map $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})\to W(k)\to W(k)/p$ (its Lie algebra splits as the direct sum of the two invertible eigen-submodules $\mathrm{lieZero}$ and $\mathrm{lieOne}$), of height $4$ (the kernel algebra of $[p]$ is finite projective of rank $p^4$ at every residue field), and with $\mathrm{lieZero}\subseteq\ker(\text{linear part of }\varpi)$. Let $M$ be a moduli package over $W(k)$: a functor $B\mapsto M(B)$ on rings $B$ with a map $W(k)\to B$ and $p$ nilpotent in $B$, assumed to satisfy the Zariski sheaf axioms (separatedness and gluing for localisations away from a family spanning the unit ideal). Let $\eta$ assign to every rigidified triple $t=(X,n_t,\rho)$ over such a $B$ — $X$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$, $n_t\in\mathbb N$, $\rho$ a pair of power series over $B/p$ — an element $\eta(t)\in M(B)$, subject to: over Noetherian bases, $\eta(t)=\eta(t')$ for admissible $t,t'$ (meaning $X$ special, of height $4$, and $\rho$ an isogeny $\bar\Phi_B\to\bar X$ of height $4n_t$) precisely when $t\cong t'$; compatibility of $\eta$ with base change along $W(k)$-algebra homomorphisms for admissible triples; and Zariski-local surjectivity of $\eta$ onto $M(B)$ by admissible triples over Noetherian bases. Given $n,m\in\mathbb N$, the conclusion asserts the existence of a scheme $X$ with a morphism $f_X\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec}(W(k)/p)$ together with, for every Noetherian $W(k)/p$-algebra $S$ in which $p$ is nilpotent, a bijection $e_S$ between the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}S\to X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(W(k)/p)$ and the set of those $x\in M(S)$ for which there is a finite family $f_1,\dots,f_r\in S$ generating the unit ideal such that over each localisation $L$ away from $f_i$ (with $p$ nilpotent in $L$) the image of $x$ equals $\eta(t)$ for some admissible rigidified triple $t$ over $L$ with $n_t=n$ and with both components of $[p^{n+m}]$ on $\bar\Phi_L$ lying in the ideal generated by the range of $t.\rho$; these bijections are compatible with base change along $W(k)/p$-algebra homomorphisms between Noetherian bases; and there are $m_P\in\mathbb N$ and a closed immersion of $X$ into $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded algebra of homogeneous polynomials in $m_P+1$ variables over $W(k)/p$ whose composite with the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}(W(k)/p)$ is $f_X$.
--
--   This is the representability of the bounded pieces $M_{n,m}$ of Drinfeld's moduli functor of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules — those rigidified triples of exponent $n$ whose isogeny $\rho$ has kernel inside $\Phi[p^{n+m}]$ — by projective schemes over $W(k)/p$, as in Boutot–Carayol II (12.2). It is the input to the local statements about the period map, which use the properness and representability to produce unique extensions of points over affine opens and to deduce injectivity of the period map.
